IMPORT prelude

-- Canada Disability Benefit Act (S.C. 2023, c. 17), with the Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35).
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. Written in the instruments' own actors and terms: "the applicant", "the beneficiary", "the
-- cohabiting spouse or common-law partner", "the Minister". The person's questions are in cdb-seat.l4, which IMPORTs
-- this module and restates no rule.
--
-- The Act is a framework: s 4 makes eligibility whatever the Regulations say, and s 5 obliges the Minister to pay "in
-- accordance with the regulations". So almost every rule here is the Regulations'.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Act ss 4, 5, 6. Regulations s 1 (definitions), s 2 (eligibility for the allocation), s 2.1 and
-- s 6.1 (the $150 supplemental amount), s 5 (approval date, 24 months back), s 6 (the basic amount, the three income-
-- tested reductions, the indexing factor), s 7 (first month), s 8(2) (lump sum of $20 or less), s 11(3) (resumption
-- after a requested suspension), ss 18-19 (reconsideration and its extension), s 37(1) (return of an overpayment).
--
-- FIGURES. The Regulations fix $2,400, $23,000, $32,500, $10,000, $14,000, 20%, 10% and $150, and index them by the
-- factor CPImax / CPI2024 (s 6(5)); the annual Consumer Price Index figures are INPUTS (Statistics Canada), except that
-- for the payment period from July 2025 the factor is 1 by the formula itself.
--
-- Edition: Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (Act last amended 2024-06-22; Regulations last amended
-- 2026-09-01), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/S.C.-2023-c.-17.txt and SOR-2025-35.txt. Unofficial
-- reproduction; not an official version. Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Canada Disability Benefit -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below zero` `x` MEANS IF `x` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `x`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` `a` `b` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- Regulations s 6(1): "rounded to the nearest cent or, if the amount is equidistant from two cents, to the higher".
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the cent` `x` MEANS (FLOOR ((`x` TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `Regulations s 6(5) -- the indexing factor`

-- s 1 "payment period": July 1 of a year to June 30 of the next. s 6(5): "CPImax / CPI2024", CPImax "the highest
-- Consumer Price Index for any calendar year beginning with 2024 and ending with the last calendar year that ended
-- before the beginning of the payment period". For the payment period beginning in July 2025 the only such year is 2024,
-- so the factor is exactly 1. For a later period the two CPI figures are inputs. The payment period is named by the year
-- in which it begins.
GIVEN `payment period beginning in` IS A NUMBER, `CPI for 2024` IS A NUMBER, `highest CPI from 2024 to the last year before the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexing factor` `payment period beginning in` `CPI for 2024` `highest CPI from 2024 to the last year before the period` MEANS
    IF `payment period beginning in` AT MOST 2025
    THEN 1
    ELSE `highest CPI from 2024 to the last year before the period` DIVIDED BY `CPI for 2024`

§§ `Regulations s 2 -- eligibility for an allocation`

-- s 2(1)(c): resident in Canada for the Income Tax Act and (i) a citizen, (ii) a permanent resident, (iii) a temporary
-- resident "who was resident in Canada for the 18 months preceding that month", (iv) a protected person, or (v) an
-- Indian under the Indian Act.
DECLARE `Status in Canada` IS ONE OF
    `a Canadian citizen`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a temporary resident resident in Canada for the previous 18 months`
    `a temporary resident resident in Canada for less than 18 months`
    `a protected person`
    `an Indian under the Indian Act`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Incarceration` IS ONE OF
    `not incarcerated`
    `in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more, but this is the first month or the month of release`
    `in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more`

-- The facts for one month. "DTC-eligible individual" is borrowed from ITA s 146.4(1) (holds a disability tax credit
-- certificate under ITA s 118.3); residence for the Income Tax Act and the filing of returns are facts.
DECLARE `CDB month` HAS
    `age in years`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `this is the month of turning 65`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a DTC-eligible individual`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in Canada for the Income Tax Act`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `status`                                                    IS A `Status in Canada`
    `incarceration`                                             IS AN `Incarceration`
    `filed a return for the last year before the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse or partner filed a return for that year`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister waived the spouse's filing condition`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment suspended at the beneficiary's request`            IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `CDB eligibility` IS ONE OF
    `eligible for an allocation this month (s 2)`
    `not eligible: under 18, or 65 or older (s 2(1)(a), (2))`
    `not eligible: not a DTC-eligible individual (s 2(1)(b))`
    `not eligible: not resident in Canada with a qualifying status (s 2(1)(c))`
    `not eligible: in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more (s 2(1)(d))`
    `not eligible: no income tax return filed for the last year (s 2(1)(e))`
    `not eligible: the cohabiting spouse or partner has not filed a return (s 2(4))`
    `not eligible: payment suspended at my request (s 2(6), s 11)`

-- s 2(1)(a): "at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age"; s 2(2): "Despite paragraph (1)(a), a person
-- is eligible ... for the month in which they turn 65". READING (finding 1): (1)(a) is read as under 65, which is the
-- only reading that leaves s 2(2) any work to do.
GIVEN `m` IS A `CDB month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the age criterion` `m` IF
        (`m`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 18 AND `m`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 65)
    OR  `m`'s `this is the month of turning 65`

GIVEN `s` IS A `Status in Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has a qualifying status` `s` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s`
    WHEN `a temporary resident resident in Canada for less than 18 months` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `m` IS A `CDB month`
GIVETH A `CDB eligibility`
`the allocation eligibility` `m` MEANS
    IF `m`'s `payment suspended at the beneficiary's request`
    THEN `not eligible: payment suspended at my request (s 2(6), s 11)`
    ELSE IF NOT (`meets the age criterion` `m`)
         THEN `not eligible: under 18, or 65 or older (s 2(1)(a), (2))`
         ELSE IF NOT (`m`'s `is a DTC-eligible individual`)
              THEN `not eligible: not a DTC-eligible individual (s 2(1)(b))`
              ELSE IF NOT (`m`'s `resident in Canada for the Income Tax Act` AND `has a qualifying status` (`m`'s `status`))
                   THEN `not eligible: not resident in Canada with a qualifying status (s 2(1)(c))`
                   ELSE IF `m`'s `incarceration` EQUALS `in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more`
                        THEN `not eligible: in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more (s 2(1)(d))`
                        ELSE IF NOT (`m`'s `filed a return for the last year before the payment period`)
                             THEN `not eligible: no income tax return filed for the last year (s 2(1)(e))`
                             ELSE IF     `m`'s `has a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner`
                                     AND (NOT (`m`'s `the spouse or partner filed a return for that year`))
                                     AND (NOT (`m`'s `the Minister waived the spouse's filing condition`))
                                  THEN `not eligible: the cohabiting spouse or partner has not filed a return (s 2(4))`
                                  ELSE `eligible for an allocation this month (s 2)`

§§ `Regulations s 6 -- the basic amount and the reduction based on income`

-- s 6(7): "adjusted income" as in ITA s 122.6 (the income of the individual and their cohabiting spouse or common-law
-- partner); "working income" as in ITA s 122.7(1) (a) and (b) plus net business income of the listed kinds. Facts from
-- the returns for the last taxation year before the payment period.
DECLARE `Household of the beneficiary` IS ONE OF
    `no cohabiting spouse or partner`
    `a cohabiting spouse or partner who is not a beneficiary`
    `a cohabiting spouse or partner who is also a beneficiary`

DECLARE `CDB income facts` HAS
    `household`                                                 IS A `Household of the beneficiary`
    `the beneficiary's own adjusted income`                     IS A NUMBER   -- C: without the spouse's income
    `the adjusted income with the current spouse or partner`    IS A NUMBER   -- E: as ITA s 122.6
    `the beneficiary's working income`                          IS A NUMBER
    `the spouse's or partner's working income`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister waived the spouse's filing condition`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6(4.1)

-- s 6(2): single: "the greater of zero and ... 20% x (C - D - ($23,000 x A))", D "the lesser of" working income and
-- "$10,000 and the indexing factor". s 6(3): spouse not a beneficiary: "20% x (E - F - ($32,500 x A))", F the lesser of
-- the couple's working income and $14,000 x A. s 6(4): spouse also a beneficiary: the same with 10%. s 6(4.1): if the
-- Minister waived the s 2(4) condition, "as if the beneficiary does not have a cohabiting spouse".
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `f` IS A `CDB income facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction based on income` `A` `f` MEANS
    LET `single` MEANS `not below zero` (20% TIMES ((`f`'s `the beneficiary's own adjusted income`) MINUS (`the lesser of` (`f`'s `the beneficiary's working income`) (10000 TIMES `A`)) MINUS (23000 TIMES `A`)))
        `couple income` MEANS (`f`'s `the adjusted income with the current spouse or partner`) MINUS (`the lesser of` ((`f`'s `the beneficiary's working income`) PLUS (`f`'s `the spouse's or partner's working income`)) (14000 TIMES `A`)) MINUS (32500 TIMES `A`)
    IN IF `f`'s `the Minister waived the spouse's filing condition`
       THEN `single`
       ELSE CONSIDER `f`'s `household`
            WHEN `no cohabiting spouse or partner` THEN `single`
            WHEN `a cohabiting spouse or partner who is not a beneficiary` THEN `not below zero` (20% TIMES `couple income`)
            WHEN `a cohabiting spouse or partner who is also a beneficiary` THEN `not below zero` (10% TIMES `couple income`)

-- s 6(1): the basic amount for a month is "(($2,400 x A) - B) / 12", rounded to the cent. READING (finding 3): a result
-- below zero is no payment; the Regulations floor only B.
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `f` IS A `CDB income facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount` `A` `f` MEANS
    `to the cent` (`not below zero` (((2400 TIMES `A`) MINUS (`the reduction based on income` `A` `f`)) DIVIDED BY 12))

-- s 8(2): "If, for a payment period, the allocation payable to a beneficiary in a month is twenty dollars or less, their
-- entire allocation for the period ... is payable as a lump sum".
GIVEN `monthly amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is paid as a lump sum for the period` `monthly amount` IF
    `monthly amount` GREATER THAN 0 AND `monthly amount` AT MOST 20

§§ `Regulations ss 2.1, 6.1 -- the supplemental amount`

-- s 2.1(1): eligible for a supplemental amount "for a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the
-- Income Tax Act that they obtain if an allocation is paid to them after they obtain the certificate and, at the time of
-- the payment, their status as a DTC-eligible individual is based on that certificate". s 6.1: "$150", paid as a lump
-- sum (s 9.1). Not indexed.
`the supplemental amount` MEANS 150

GIVEN `obtained an ITA 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `an allocation was paid after obtaining it` IS A BOOLEAN, `DTC status at that payment rests on that certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the supplemental amount payable` `obtained an ITA 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) certificate` `an allocation was paid after obtaining it` `DTC status at that payment rests on that certificate` MEANS
    IF `obtained an ITA 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) certificate` AND `an allocation was paid after obtaining it` AND `DTC status at that payment rests on that certificate`
    THEN `the supplemental amount`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Regulations ss 5, 7 -- from when the allocation is paid`

-- s 5(1): the application is "deemed to be approved ... on the earliest day on which an applicant becomes eligible";
-- (2): not earlier than "the day that is 24 months before the day on which the application is made". s 7: "The month
-- following the month in which a beneficiary's application is approved ... is the first month". Counted in months back
-- from the month of application; the answer is how many months before the application month the first allocation
-- month is (negative: after it). READING: months, not days, for the 24 months.
GIVEN `months between first becoming eligible and applying` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months before the application that the allocation starts` `months between first becoming eligible and applying` MEANS
    (`the lesser of` `months between first becoming eligible and applying` 24) MINUS 1

§§ `Regulative rules -- the applicant's duties, and what the Minister owes`

DECLARE `CDB party` IS ONE OF `the applicant or beneficiary`, `the Minister`

DECLARE `CDB act` IS ONE OF
    `provide the information the Minister requires`
    `return the overpayment`
    `request a reconsideration`
    `reconsider and notify the decision with reasons`
    `request an extension of the time to ask for a reconsideration`
    `request resumption of payment`

-- Act s 6: "An applicant or the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their own affairs must
-- provide the Minister with any information that the Minister may require in respect of the application." No period.
GIVEN `the Minister has required information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CDB party` `CDB act`
DECIDE `Act s 6 -- an applicant must give the Minister the information required` IS
    IF `the Minister has required information`
    THEN PARTY `the applicant or beneficiary`
         MUST  `provide the information the Minister requires`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Regulations s 37(1): a person who received a payment "to which the person ... is not entitled, or ... in excess ...
-- must return the amount ... as soon as feasible". (4): no interest. No period.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CDB party` `CDB act`
DECIDE `Regulations s 37(1) -- a person overpaid must return the overpayment as soon as feasible` IS
    PARTY `the applicant or beneficiary`
    MUST  `return the overpayment`

-- Regulations s 18(1): a dissatisfied person "may, within 180 days after the day on which the person is notified in
-- writing of the decision, make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration". (4): the Minister "must, within a
-- reasonable time, reconsider ... and ... must notify in writing ... of the Minister's decision and the reasons for it".
-- "A reasonable time" is no number of days.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CDB party` `CDB act`
DECIDE `Regulations s 18 -- I may ask for a reconsideration within 180 days, and the Minister must then reconsider and give reasons` IS
    PARTY `the applicant or beneficiary`
    MAY   `request a reconsideration`
    WITHIN 180
    HENCE PARTY `the Minister`
          MUST  `reconsider and notify the decision with reasons`

-- Regulations s 19(1): "A person may request that the Minister extend the 180-day period ... not later than 185 days
-- after the end of that period." Clock: days from the end of the 180 days. (3): the Minister "must allow" it for a
-- listed situation (emergency, disaster, civil disturbance, disruption of public services, serious accident, injury or
-- illness, emotional or mental distress).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CDB party` `CDB act`
DECIDE `Regulations s 19(1) -- I may ask for more time within 185 days after the 180 days end` IS
    PARTY `the applicant or beneficiary`
    MAY   `request an extension of the time to ask for a reconsideration`
    WITHIN 185

-- Regulations s 11(3): after a suspension at the beneficiary's request, they "may request in writing that the Minister
-- resume payment ... within 24 months after the date of suspension. If no request ... is received within that period,
-- the allocation is deemed to have ceased and they must make a new application". Clock: days; 24 months as 730 days
-- (READING).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CDB party` `CDB act`
DECIDE `Regulations s 11(3) -- after asking for a suspension, I may ask for payment to resume within 24 months` IS
    PARTY `the applicant or beneficiary`
    MAY   `request resumption of payment`
    WITHIN 730
